Hi,

I'am testing the buildroot system I created with VirtualBox.
I used the build-ext3-script to create a harddisk image that I converted
using qemu-img and VBoxManage.

During the startup I always get the following kernel message:
VFS: Mounted root (ext3 filesystem) readonly on device 3:1.

I was already looking in the buildroot configuration but I couldn't find
any option to set if the filesystem is read-only or writeable.

Is the filesystem made writeable by the buildroot, busybox or the linux
configuration?
Where can I make the filesystem writeable?

